<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- The downloads page of anti-lang.com. Step 9 of ./r fills the marks
     and rsyncs the page to the webroot. Every package it names is an
     asset of the GitHub release, and this site serves none of them. It
     serves the signature of the manifest and the public key. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Anti @VERSION@</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --txt: #fff1c8;
      --txt-dim: rgba(255, 241, 200, .78);
      --amber: #ffb000;
      --glow: rgba(255, 176, 0, .75);
    }
    html { height: 100%; }
    body {
      min-height: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 3rem 1rem; box-sizing: border-box;
      display: grid; place-items: start center;
      background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f5f0e1 0%, #c9a77c 55%, #5b3a21 100%);
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    }
    .terminal {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden;
      width: min(52rem, 94vw); padding: 2.25rem 2.5rem 2.75rem;
      border-radius: 1rem; background: #1a1206;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255, 176, 0, .55);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px #2b1d0c, 0 24px 60px rgba(40, 20, 0, .45),
                  inset 0 0 90px rgba(255, 140, 0, .08);
    }
    .terminal, .terminal * {
      color: var(--txt);
      text-shadow: 0 0 max(5px, .21em) rgba(255, 176, 0, .85),
                   0 0 .46em var(--glow),
                   0 0 .96em rgba(255, 176, 0, .35);
    }
    .terminal::after {
      content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none;
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, .18) 0 1px,
                                            transparent 1px 3px);
      mix-blend-mode: multiply;
    }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: 1.9rem; }
    h2 { margin: 2rem 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    p, li, td, th { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    p { margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
    .dim { color: var(--txt-dim); }
    a { color: var(--amber); }
    pre {
      margin: 0 0 1rem; padding: .85rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 176, 0, .35); border-radius: .5rem;
      background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .35);
    }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
    th, td {
      padding: .4rem .5rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 176, 0, .25);
    }
    td.digest { word-break: break-all; font-size: .8rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="terminal">
    <h1>Anti @VERSION@</h1>
    <p class="dim">Released @RELEASED@. One command installs the compiler,
      the runtime archive, the standard library and the LLVM tools into
      your own account. The package carries the sysroot of every target, so
      nothing else is downloaded, and nothing outside your home directory
      is written.</p>

    <h2>Install on macOS and Linux</h2>
    <pre>curl -fsSL https://anti-lang.com/install.sh | bash</pre>

    <h2>Install on Windows</h2>
    <pre>irm https://anti-lang.com/install.ps1 | iex</pre>

    <h2>Packages</h2>
    <p>The installer downloads the package of your platform and
      <code>SHA256SUMS</code> from the
      <a href="@RELEASE@">GitHub release of @TAG@</a>, and
      <a href="@SIGNATURE@"><code>SHA256SUMS.sig</code></a> from this site.
      It checks the signature against the public key it carries, and then
      the digest of the package against the manifest. It unpacks the
      package, runs <code>antic --version</code> and
      <code>anti --version</code> from it as the check of the install, and
      puts the two programs on your path. It runs nothing else.</p>
    <p>The two halves stand on two hosts on purpose. Whoever takes GitHub
      changes binaries that the signature no longer covers. Whoever takes
      this site signs nothing, because the private key is on neither host.
      A release is genuine only when both agree.</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Target</th><th>Package</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
@ROWS@
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Manual install on macOS and Linux</h2>
    <p>The same steps as commands, with the name of your package from the
      table. The two <code>openssl</code> lines are the signature check of
      the installers, and <code>shasum</code> reads the manifest. Linux
      spells the last of those <code>sha256sum --ignore-missing -c
      SHA256SUMS</code>.</p>
    <pre>package=anti-@VERSION@-macos-arm64.tar.xz
curl -fsSLO @DOWNLOAD@/$package
curl -fsSLO @DOWNLOAD@/SHA256SUMS
curl -fsSLO @SIGNATURE@
curl -fsSLO @KEY@
openssl dgst -sha256 -binary -out SHA256SUMS.sha256 SHA256SUMS
openssl pkeyutl -verify -pubin -inkey release.pem -in SHA256SUMS.sha256 -sigfile SHA256SUMS.sig
shasum -a 256 --ignore-missing -c SHA256SUMS
mkdir -p ~/.local/share ~/.local/bin
tar -xJf $package -C ~/.local/share
cp ~/.local/share/anti/bin/antic ~/.local/share/anti/bin/anti ~/.local/bin/
antic --version
anti --version</pre>

    <h2>Manual install on Windows</h2>
    <p>The same in PowerShell. <code>openssl</code> is the one of Git for
      Windows, and <code>Get-FileHash</code> gives the digest the manifest
      line has to hold.</p>
    <pre>$package = "anti-@VERSION@-windows-x86_64.tar.xz"
irm @DOWNLOAD@/$package -OutFile $package
irm @DOWNLOAD@/SHA256SUMS -OutFile SHA256SUMS
irm @SIGNATURE@ -OutFile SHA256SUMS.sig
irm @KEY@ -OutFile release.pem
openssl dgst -sha256 -binary -out SHA256SUMS.sha256 SHA256SUMS
openssl pkeyutl -verify -pubin -inkey release.pem -in SHA256SUMS.sha256 -sigfile SHA256SUMS.sig
(Get-FileHash $package -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower() -eq ((Select-String -SimpleMatch $package SHA256SUMS).Line -split " ")[0]
tar.exe -xJf $package -C $env:LOCALAPPDATA
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\anti\bin"
Copy-Item "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\anti\bin\antic.exe", "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\anti\bin\anti.exe" "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\anti\bin"
&amp; "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\anti\bin\antic.exe" --version
&amp; "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\anti\bin\anti.exe" --version</pre>

    <h2>The public key</h2>
    <p>The installers carry the public key of the release and check every
      manifest against it. The same key stands at
      <a href="/keys/release.pem">/keys/release.pem</a>, so a second source
      of it is one fetch away. Its SHA-256 fingerprint is:</p>
    <pre>@FINGERPRINT@</pre>
    <p class="dim">The key is the trust anchor of every Anti download.
      The same key signs the LLVM tools of
      <a href="https://github.com/anti-lang/llvm-tools">anti-lang/llvm-tools</a>.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
